## 2026-11-10 - Prevent accidental hiding of the essential toolbar

- An isolated context-menu event reproduced Qt's native Main checkbox and
  visibility action before the production change. Disabling toolbar movement
  does not prevent hiding through that menu.
- MainWindow.createPopupMenu now returns None. This removes the default
  main-window visibility popup, not the normal editing menus in text controls.
  No new setting, layout migration or configuration reset is introduced.
- Eight focused cases cover Tutorial/toolbar context events, native field
  editing and reopening an older hidden toolbar in both themes. All 167
  cases across the five GUI suites passed with native exit zero. Black/Ruff
  passed the two changed Python files; mypy passed ten GUI source files.
- Updated seven affected guides without regenerating unchanged screenshots.
  Recovery is a manual reopen after finishing the current run and saving
  editor changes; an existing instance does not hot-load the fix.
- The first scoped tracking preview correctly rejected an omitted Publication
  field without remote writes. Corrected the declaration and passed preview.
  Independent completion verified lea-21/#21 CLOSED/COMPLETED, exact managed
  content, one Done item and persistent backlink. Settled apply returned one
  no-op without content/timestamp churn; all twenty older records and original
  #2/#9 review gaps remain unchanged.
- Final preservation retains 53 unrelated public fingerprints, all fifteen
  media hashes, selected private/native metadata, HEAD and empty staging.
- Checks use fictional temporary state and INI settings. The independently
  opened user GUI is not a test fixture and is neither inspected nor driven.
  Sources remain local; no build, release, commit, push or live action.

## 2026-11-09 - Live per-command desktop metrics

- Started lea-20 to make current-command outcomes visible while the console
  runs. Trace actual confirmed applications, inspected jobs, skips, failures,
  hiring-message/draft outcomes and connection invitations rather than
  inferring them from human log text.
- Preserve the shared source checkout's existing changes and the independently
  running user instance. All development checks use fictional disposable state;
  no live automation, user-process manipulation or source/release publication.
- Added strict Qt-free snapshots, a bounded framed stream and optional
  authoritative engine hooks. The GUI opts in only its own child, removes
  frames from human output and reports malformed/truncated data without
  exposing rejected payloads or clearing valid totals. Ordinary CLI/file
  logging remains unchanged.
- Five color-coded cards expose job outcomes and actual hiring-message sends.
  Standalone Connect uses profile/invitation outcomes. Secondary totals keep
  drafts, completed dry runs, uncertainty and invitations distinct. Targets
  follow the actual child phase; elapsed time starts on process-start and
  freezes at finish. Clear log/theme/selector edits retain totals; only an
  accepted new command resets them. Failed startup does not invent zeroes.
- Submission observation precedes outreach approval and existing persistence.
  The display is ephemeral, not a transactional ledger or delivery receipt;
  interruption can leave live totals ahead of the database/final summary.
  This task does not change application/outreach durability.
- Early compact checks exposed both missing fonts and actual header clipping.
  Reused capture font registration in window tests, tightened running-state
  geometry, compressed spacing and made the caption wrap when narrow. All
  four compact/expanded dark/light cases then passed without shrinking digits
  or weakening width assertions.
- The final affected integration passed 308 cases with native exit zero.
  The first full attempt passed 307 with one incorrect media-fixture assertion:
  a Reapply-only checkbox retained its value when Connect was selected.
  Corrected only the assertion's action guard. Black/Ruff passed fifteen
  scoped Python files; mypy passed sixteen source files including capture
  tooling after replacing ambiguous Qt API spellings with typed equivalents.
- Updated thirteen affected guides, retaining the concise README. Run-only
  capture refreshes seven PNGs/one GIF; its explicit fictional snapshots
  start neither a process nor a timer. The Run GIF remains nine frames and
  17.8 seconds. Directly inspected compact light and expanded dark stills;
  geometry checks separately cover both sizes/themes. These are offscreen
  fixtures, not a native installed-release or live-site acceptance claim.
- Pre-bookkeeping immutable-baseline checks preserve thirty public fingerprints,
  nineteen older durable mappings, selected private/native metadata, HEAD
  and the empty staged diff. No private contents/registry values were read
  for that comparison. Prior console/tooltips/README work remains intact.
- Final preservation retains twenty-eight unrelated fingerprints and allows
  the index/ledger completion updates explicitly. All fifteen media hashes
  still match qualification. Reviewed the Run GIF's first frame as well as
  the two stills, not a complete animation replay.
- Scoped preview/apply and independent read-back verify lea-20/#20
  CLOSED/COMPLETED, exact managed content, one Done issue-backed Project item
  and persistent backlink. Settled apply produced one no-op with unchanged
  remote/local content and timestamps. All nineteen older issues/items/
  mappings and original #2/#9 OPEN/In review gaps remain intact. Final
  bookkeeping wording was separately previewed/applied and read back;
  another settled no-op verified no content or timestamp churn. The first
  settlement receipt is retained separately rather than overwritten.
  Sources remain local and uncommitted; existing release binaries and the
  independently running user window are untouched.

Status: CONTINUOUS_LEDGER
Milestone: Evidence-grounded repository engineering history
Dependencies: None

## Purpose
Keep dated technical decisions and verification receipts without inventing user
approval or publishing private continuity. This perpetual ledger is not an issue.

## Tasks
- Append meaningful engineering outcomes and actual failures.
- Attribute old evidence without representing it as newly run validation.
- Keep target qualification, human acceptance and publication distinct.

## Acceptance criteria
- Receipts describe observed outcomes and explicit remaining limitations.
- Raw requests, applicant values, private artifacts and credentials stay outside this ledger.

## Completion evidence
Ongoing record; individual bounded outcomes belong to numbered workstreams.

## Completion log

